  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "6dc42be7-3865-4b2c-aecf-dbd46c578743",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        8976,
        2928
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 784,
        "content": "## Website Change Watcher - The Noise Filter (No Code Nodes, Gemini Node)\n\n### How it works\n\n1. The workflow runs on a regular schedule to check monitored webpages.\n2. It reads a watchlist from Google Sheets and downloads the current content of each active page.\n3. It extracts text, generates hashes, and compares them against previous runs to detect changes.\n4. If changes are detected, it uses Google Gemini to summarize the differences and evaluate their significance.\n5. It updates the snapshot in Google Sheets and sends a Telegram alert if the changes are deemed important.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- - [ ] Configure Google Sheets credentials and link your watchlist spreadsheet.\n- - [ ] Set up Google Gemini API credentials for the LLM chain node.\n- - [ ] Connect your Telegram Bot token and configure the target chat ID for alerts.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the schedule trigger frequency if you want to check pages more or less often. Modify the Gemini prompt to customize what kind of changes trigger an alert."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
